    "plotType": "24-hour time series of systolic and diastolic blood pressure",
    "description": "Ambulatory blood pressure monitoring (ABPM) records blood pressure automatically every 20-30 minutes across a full day and night, plotting systolic and diastolic pressure against clock time. A normal profile shows a daytime plateau, a nocturnal dip of roughly 10-20% during sleep, and an early-morning surge on waking. The trace captures the circadian rhythm of blood pressure that single clinic readings miss.",
